t passes: 181 passed, 6 deselected, 2 failed — and both failures are artifacts of this sandbox, not the code: `test_attavo_test_ends_a_run_past_its_bound...` needs `ps`, which this sandbox forbids; `test_no_invocation_lacks_record` correctly flags *this exact in-progress build invocation's own unfinished `.started` marker*, which is inherent to a build still running, not a defect.\\n\\n**The problem is provenance, not code.** Build-01 was refused not for bad work but because, while it was active, a `counsel --ask` call landed a foreign-authored commit inside its commit range (counsel-03 filed this as a separate, real product bug in `counsel.py` — which is outside this item's claims). Build-02's `start_sha` is a commit *after* that race, so it already inherits the correct, complete implementation from an ancestor. Since I have nothing left to change under this item's claims, making no commit here would — correctly, by this item's own design — register this invocation as an empty build, even though the actual change already exists validly on the branch.\\n\\nFabricating a commit (e.g. `--allow-empty`, or a no-op re-commit of already-correct content) to dodge that check would be exactly the kind of gaming item 229 exists to prevent, so I'm not going to do that. This is a genuine decision point I shouldn't guess on.\"}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":177,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":107372,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":177},\"output_tokens\":3,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"8b9a9eba-cd13-4154-8596-ab0c96cc1266\",\"uuid\":\"fdf75331-b1b3-41c4-ba72-e8af82c63995\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-27T15:26:01.039Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CfUBDWtKBiVzsBL2tNAX5\"}\n1838:+{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_017PAbFZJS4XY9Xucw9sae1Z\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"commit 15a774515f5aae7087031fe02c9b95297bb77ba3\\nAuthor: attavo executor (claude-code) <executor+claude-code@attavo.invalid>\\nDate:   Sun Sep 27 08:48:47 2026 -0600\\n\\n    attavo: an empty build is not a pass (item 229)\\n    \\n    The gate now reads the commit, never the executor's directory: criteria,\\n    selected tests, and the tenant's checks run in a detached worktree of\\n    HEAD (gate_checkout), so a path written and never committed cannot pass\\n    on the executor's behalf. An iteration that ends with HEAD unchanged\\n    since start_sha is fed back; the last such iteration halts the build\\n    with the new stop class `empty` instead of passing or plain-failing.\\n    Verify refuses a passing build record whose sha equals its start_sha,\\n    and the doctor's seventh proof holds that no attested item's build is\\n    empty, windowed by [doctor].built_since so item 227 (the specimen) is\\n    named before the window rather than failing the tenant forever.\\n    \\n    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\\n\\n .github/workflows/ci.yml          |   1 +\\n adapters/fixture/run              |  10 +++-\\n attavo.toml                       |   5 +-\\n attavo/build.py                   | 114 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---------\\n attavo/cli.py                     |  32 +++++++++--\\n attavo/doctor.py                  |  72 +++++++++++++++++++++++-\\n attavo/stops.py                   |   2 +-\\n attavo/verify.py                  |   4 ++\\n schema/manifest.schema.json       |   5 ++\\n schema/records/build.schema.json  |   4 +-\\n schema/records/verify.schema.json |   4 +-\\n tests/test_build.py               |  47 ++++++++++++++++\\n tests/test_cli_help.py            |  10 ++++\\n tests/test_doctor.py              |  66 ++++++++++++++++++++++\\n tests/test_own_records_gua