ular attempt's start_sha (item 229), so a\\n+    retried attempt whose head already carries a prior attempt's valid\\n+    commits owes no commit of its own; an attempt that ends on the\\n+    approved tree, whatever it left in the working directory, is empty\\n+    regardless of how it got there. Scoped to claims rather than\\n+    \\\"everything outside paths.records\\\", so a commit that lands between\\n+    approval and this attempt's start but touches no claimed path --\\n+    a tenant installing an adapter, say -- never rescues or defeats the\\n+    comparison on its own account; every commit an executor's own loop\\n+    ever lands is already confined to claims (this module's own boundary\\n+    check above), so a real prior attempt's work is always visible here.\\n+    None when either commit does not resolve in this repository -- not\\n+    known, not asserted.\\\"\\\"\\\"\\n+    for commit in (approval_sha, sha):\\n+        resolved = subprocess.run([\\\"git\\\", \\\"-C\\\", str(root), \\\"cat-file\\\", \\\"-e\\\", f\\\"{commit}^{{commit}}\\\"],\\n+                                  capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\\n+        if resolved.returncode != 0:\\n+            return None\\n+    pathspec = claims if claims else [\\\".\\\"]\\n+    out = subprocess.run([\\\"git\\\", \\\"-C\\\", str(root), \\\"diff\\\", \\\"--quiet\\\", approval_sha, sha,\\n+                          \\\"--\\\", *pathspec], capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\\n+    if out.returncode not in (0, 1):\\n+        return None\\n+    return out.returncode == 0\\n+\\n+\\n def protected_path_touched(root: Path, start_sha: str, records_rel: str,\\n                            specs_rel: str) -> str | None:\\n     \\\"\\\"\\\"The first path an executor's own commits touched under\\n\",\"exit_code\":0,\"status\":\"completed\"}}\n5346:+grep -q \"names no change\" \"$tmp/verify.out\"\n5382:+grep -q \"^def test_no_attested_item_is_empty(\" tests/test_doctor.py\n5430:+assert \"the executor committed nothing\" in r[\"stop\"][\"detail\"], r[\"stop\"]\n5433:+grep -q \"you committed nothing\" records/1/build-01.log\n5454:+The gate reads the commit. Each iteration's criteria, selected tests and tenant checks run in a detached worktree of `HEAD` (`gate_checkout`: `git worktree add --detach`, removed when the iteration's gate is done), never in the executor's directory. A file written and not committed cannot pass a criterion, a test or a check on the executor's behalf; a tenant checks command that writes beside itself writes into the worktree and is gone with it. The pre-executor probe (`[checks].probe`) still runs against the approved tree in place, as it did.\n5456:+An empty iteration is told so. When an iteration ends with `HEAD` equal to `start_sha`, the gate runs (on the approved tree, where the criteria already fail), the log and the feedback both carry \"you committed nothing: no commit since <start>; N path(s) modified or untracked in the working tree, which the gate does not read\" and \"commit your work; the gate reads the commit, not the tree\", and the loop continues. An executor that answers `done` before committing on its first iteration and commits on its second passes as before (`test_an_empty_iteration_is_fed_back_and_a_later_commit_passes`).\n5458:+An empty build is halted. A build is empty when the tree its record names is the approved tree outside `paths.records`: `git diff --quiet <approval sha> HEAD -- . ':!<records>'` finds nothing. The comparison is against the approval, not the attempt's own `start_sha`, so a retried attempt whose head already carries a prior attempt's valid commits adopts them and owes no commit of its own; an attempt that ends on the approved tree, whatever it left in the working directory, is what #227 was. When the last iteration ends empty, the record is `halted` with a new stop class `empty`, provenance `executor`, detail \"the executor committed nothing; ...\" with the count of paths left in the tree; an earlier empty iteration is fed back and the loop continues. The class is the executor's, so counsel reads it and a steer retries it under R3; no new family. `STOP_CLASSES` and the build and verify schemas carry `empty` (build/9, verify/8). The status can never be `pass` on the approved tree.\n5460:+Verify refuses an empty build. A passing build record whose tree is the approved tree outside `paths.records` is refused before any adapter runs: \"the latest build record names no change; nothing to review\". The build no longer writes such a record; the refusal is verify's own guard against any record shaped this way, whoever wrote it.\n5466:+The stub under `stub/` is the change: `gate_checkout` and the empty-iteration handling in `attavo/build.py`, the class in `attavo/stops.py` and the two schemas, verify's refusal, proof seven and the manifest key, the fixture adapter's `ATTAVO_FIXTURE_NO_COMMIT`, the self-tenant's window and deselect, and seven tests red on the tree (v0.29.0). `tests/test_cli_help.py::test_help_names_the_seventh_proof_and_the_empty_stop` is red on the stub by design; the help text is the build's. Four existing tests move with the gate: two in `tests/test_testtool.py` whose checks counter lived in the tree the gate no longer reads, `test_self_tenancy.py`'s assertion that the manifest has no `[doctor]` table, `test_own_records_guard.py`'s deselect count, and `test_stub_ratio.py`'s pinned `verify/7`. `python3 -m mypy` exits 0 on the stub.\n5498:+- an-executor-that-commits-nothing-does-not-pass.sh: on a fixture tenant whose executor writes the change into the tree and never commits, `attavo build 1` ends halted with stop class `empty`, provenance `executor`, `sha` equal to `start_sha`, every criterion non-zero, the log saying the executor committed nothing and that the gate reads the commit, and `attavo verify 1` refuses the halted build with no review record written\n5565:+          --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_attested_item_is_empty\n5884:+run = \"xargs -r python3 -m pytest -q --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_every_gate_rejects --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_one_item_traversed_every_stage --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_commit_lacks_a_record --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_stop_lacks_cause --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_every_attested_item_is_sealed --deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_attested_item_is_empty\"\n6199:+def gate_checkout(root: Path) -> Iterator[Path]:\n6446:+            # An executor that committed nothing built nothing, whatever it\n6478:+            with gate_checkout(root) as gate_root:\n6526:+                transcripts[-1] += (\"\\nyou committed nothing: \" + empty_line +\n6539:+                    empty_detail = f\"the executor committed nothing; {empty_line}\"\n6546:+                feedback_lines += [\"you committed nothing: \" + empty_line,\n7444:+def proof_no_attested_item_is_empty(root: Path, m: dict[str, Any] | None) -> Proof:\n7448:+    merged and sealed, and its build committed nothing -- the executor\n7521:+            proof_no_attested_item_is_empty(root, m)]\n8134:+        print(\"attavo verify: refused: the latest build record names no change \"\n9868:+# change into the working tree, committed nothing, and answered done; the\n9882:+    assert \"the executor committed nothing\" in rec[\"stop\"][\"detail\"], rec[\"stop\"]\n9888:+    assert \"you committed nothing\" in log and \"the gate reads the commit, not the tree\" in log, log\n10012:+    for phrase in (\"no attested item is empty\", \"built_since\", \"committed nothing\", \"reads the commit\"):\n10967:+# over an attested item whose build committed nothing. ---\n11023:+def test_no_attested_item_is_empty() -> None:\n11236:+    \"--deselect tests/test_doctor.py::test_no_attested_item_is_empty\",\n12406:+    assert \"names no change\" in run.stdout and \"sha equals start_sha\" in run.stdout, run.stdout\n12466:diff --git a/tests/test_build.py b/tests/test_build.py\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
