rojects/attest/adapters/codex/run:701:# on this adapter's own report line, the same way non-question already\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/codex/run:703:# counsel run on a stop the definition of done never touches.\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/codex/run:722:    split out from report_fields so a retry's first, discarded call\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/codex/run:723:    still counts (issue #88: a non-question costs two executor turns,\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/codex/run:789:    # a question the executor answers on the first call otherwise never\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/codex/run:829:    status = final.get(\"status\", \"done\")\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/codex/run:830:    question = final.get(\"question\")\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/codex/run:831:    cls = question_class(status, question)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/codex/run:837:        # Issue #88, class A: a report in the question channel is\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/codex/run:854:        status2 = final2.get(\"status\", \"done\")\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/codex/run:855:        question2 = final2.get(\"question\")\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/codex/run:856:        cls2 = question_class(status2, question2)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/codex/run:861:        # A non-question costs two executor turns, not one: sum both\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/codex/run:863:        # whatever the retry's own outcome. cost_usd stays null (issue\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/codex/run:874:            # tell it apart from a genuine question.\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/codex/run:875:            print(\"adapters/codex/run: halted: class non-question -- the \"\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/codex/run:877:            line = {**common2, \"status\": \"question\", \"question\": question2,\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/codex/run:878:                   \"class\": \"non-question\"}\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/codex/run:882:        line = {**common2, \"status\": status2, \"question\": question2}\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/adapters/codex/run:887:    line = {**common, \"status\": status, \"question\": question}\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:24:    retry_after_s,\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:56:def commit_record(root: Path, record_paths: Path | list[Path], message: str) -> None:\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:57:    \"\"\"`git commit --only` on every record path given, and each one's .log\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:59:    commit that sweeps the index is exactly the regression issue #46\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:62:    (issue #89) is committed alongside the record it names, in the same\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:63:    commit and the same push, so a second worktree or a fresh clone reads\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:67:    commit as the stage record it counsels. Authored and committed as\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:69:    config, so a driven item's record commits are never indistinguishable\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:89:    git(root, \"commit\", \"--only\", \"-m\", message, *paths, env=env)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:92:def push_record_commit(root: Path, branch: str) -> tuple[bool, str | None]:\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:96:    commit just wrote already names. This is the record push's own retry\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:110:        return False, f\"push rejected and the retry merge failed: {pull.stderr.strip() or err}\"\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:123:    no retry: this is the lease the marker commit takes on the attempt it\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:132:    the loser: it says so, resets its own marker commit, and starts\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:151:    or a scratch checkout with none is not a refusal; a pass commits\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:194:# never committed and never among the paths commit_record ever names. ---\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:265:    bound: str | None = None  # R3: \"stall\" or \"ceiling\" when cls is \"hung\"\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:274:    \"\"\"R3: whether stage's adapter declares it streams events at all\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:305:    R3: the stage's own ceiling (wall clock from the marker's own `at`)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:337:def uncommitted_record(root: Path, records_dir: Path, stage: str) -> Path | None:\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:339:    no commit for yet -- the moment between a worker's write and its own\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:340:    commit. None when the latest record is already committed, or there\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:355:    working tree carries that git has not committed yet. Scoped to the\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:357:    operator's own spec-gate or approve, routinely uncommitted between\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:363:    return (uncommitted_record(root, records_dir, \"build\") is not None\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:364:           or uncommitted_record(root, records_dir, \"verify\") is not None)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:369:    anything else -- a commit landed there from elsewhere (an approval\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:373:    a detached child is still writing into would corrupt its own commits.\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:375:    also carries its own commits origin has not seen yet (an operator's\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:377:    tip instead -- no merge commit, and the marker this pass is about to\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:410:    file-stops on a non-pass record (issue #100, #89), one `git commit\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:411:    --only`, one push with the record push's own merge retry. The\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:412:    marker is the pass's, already committed and pushed before this\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:448:    to_commit = [after]\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:451:        state = retry_state(root, m, records_dir, stage, stop.get(\"class\"),\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:453:        # R3: a stop the next plain pass would already retry -- now, or\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:459:        # or the class was never a plain retry's to begin with.\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:465:                to_commit.append(counsel_after)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:474:        commit_record(root, to_commit, message)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:476:        print(f\"attavo drive: stopped: could not commit the {stage} record: {exc}\")\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:480:        ok, err = push_record_commit(root, branch)\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:485:        print(f\"attavo drive: note: no origin remote; {after.name} is committed, not pushed\")\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:488:        question = (record.get(\"halted\") or {}).get(\"question\")\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:489:        print(f\"attavo drive: stopped: {stage} halted: {question} ({after.name}); \"\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:527:    \"\"\"The lease (ruling A): the marker, committed and pushed as a plain\n/Users/davidbean/Projects/attest/attavo/drive.py:528:    